<Base title="How We Source: Our Editorial Standard" description="Every claim on this site traces to a named source with a date. Here is the standard we hold ourselves to." breadcrumbs={[{name:"How we source", url:"/sources/"}]}>
  <div class="wrap"><article>
    <span class="eyebrow">Editorial standard</span>
    <h1>How we source</h1>
    <div class="answer"><b>The short answer</b>Every factual claim on this site traces to a named source with a date. Tier 1 means the cruise line&rsquo;s own published material. Tier 2 means an established cruise-news outlet. If we cannot verify a number, we leave it out and say so.</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why we publish our sources at all</h2>
      <p>Most cruise advice online repeats figures that were true two years ago. Drink prices move. Package pricing moves. Loyalty thresholds move. A confident number with no date attached is the most common way cruise content goes wrong, and you have no way to check it.</p>
      <p>So we show the work. Every review and guide ends with the list of sources behind it, each one named and dated, so you can check any claim yourself.</p>
      <h2>What the tiers mean</h2>
      <p><strong>Tier 1</strong> is the cruise line speaking for itself: a published benefit grid, a press release, an earnings release, an SEC filing. <strong>Tier 2</strong> is an established cruise-news outlet reporting something we could not get from the line directly, such as a quote from an earnings call.</p>
      <p>Where a claim carries real weight and we could only find one outlet for it, we say so in the video and on the page rather than presenting it as settled.</p>
      <h2>We correct ourselves in public</h2>
      <p>When a figure we used before turns out to be stale, we say that plainly on the page instead of quietly swapping the number. Our Crown &amp; Anchor coverage does exactly that with a beverage package price that no longer holds.</p>
      <h2>Freshness</h2>
      <p>Every page carries the date it was last checked. Guides get re-checked on a schedule, and anything price-sensitive gets re-verified before we republish.</p>
      <h2>Sponsorship</h2>
      <p>Sponsored segments are labelled on the page and disclosed on the video. A sponsor never influences a verdict, and no sponsor sees a post before it publishes.</p>
    </div>
  </article></div>
</Base>
